🧠 Correct Architecture (Final, Clean)
1️⃣ Global Editor Injection (Every Page)

You do NOT attach the editor per page.

You inject it once at the root.

// App.tsx
<EditorProvider>
  <EditorOverlay />   {/* floating toggle + inspector */}
  <Router />
</EditorProvider>


This guarantees:

Editor exists everywhere

No routing logic

No page-specific setup

2️⃣ Editor Toggle (Manual, Explicit)

You control edit mode yourself, not via auth.

Examples:

Keyboard shortcut: Ctrl + Shift + E

Floating button: “Edit UI”

Dev-only flag (optional)

isEditing: boolean


Nothing blocks it. Nothing hides it.

